<title identifier="/us/usc/t99"><num value="99">Title 99—</num><heading>SAMPLE PROVISIONS</heading>
<note topic="miscellaneous"><p>Current through 119-124</p></note>
<chapter identifier="/us/usc/t99/ch1"><num value="1">CHAPTER 1—</num><heading>GENERAL RULES</heading>
<section identifier="/us/usc/t99/s1"><num value="1">§ 1.</num><heading> Vacation of awards</heading><subsection class="indent0" identifier="/us/usc/t99/s1/a"><num value="a">(a)</num><chapeau> In any of the following cases the court may vacate the award—</chapeau><paragraph class="indent1" identifier="/us/usc/t99/s1/a/1"><num value="1">(1)</num><content> where the award was procured by <ref href="/us/usc/t5/s580">fraud</ref>; or</content>
</paragraph>
<paragraph class="indent1" identifier="/us/usc/t99/s1/a/2"><num value="2">(2)</num><content> where the arbitrators exceeded their powers.</content>
</paragraph>
<continuation class="indent0">The court shall state its reasons.</continuation>
</subsection>
<subsection class="indent0" identifier="/us/usc/t99/s1/b"><num value="b">(b)</num><content> A rehearing may be directed as the court sets <ref class="footnoteRef" idref="fn1">1</ref><note type="footnote" id="fn1"><num>1</num> So in original. Probably should be “sets forth”.</note> in its order.</content>
</subsection>
<sourceCredit>(<ref href="/us/act/1947-07-30/ch392">July 30, 1947, ch. 392</ref>, <ref href="/us/stat/61/672">61 Stat. 672</ref>; <ref href="/us/pl/101/552/s5">Pub. L. 101–552, § 5</ref>, <date date="1990-11-15">Nov. 15, 1990</date>, <ref href="/us/stat/104/2745">104 Stat. 2745</ref>.)</sourceCredit>
<notes type="uscNote">
<note role="crossHeading" topic="editorialNotes"><heading><b>Editorial Notes</b></heading></note>
<note topic="amendments"><heading>Amendments</heading><p class="indent0">1990—<ref href="/us/pl/101/552">Pub. L. 101–552</ref> designated existing provisions as subsec. (a).</p>
</note>
<note role="crossHeading" topic="statutoryNotes"><heading><b>Statutory Notes and Related Subsidiaries</b></heading></note>
<note topic="effectiveDateOfAmendment"><heading>Effective Date of 1990 Amendment</heading><p class="indent0">Amendment effective on date of enactment.</p></note>
</notes>
</section>
<section identifier="/us/usc/t99/s2"><num value="2">§ 2.</num><heading> Allocation of duties</heading><subsection class="indent2 firstIndent-2" identifier="/us/usc/t99/s2/a"><num value="a">(a)</num><heading> In general</heading><chapeau class="indent1">The Architect shall have charge of work that affects—</chapeau><paragraph class="indent2" identifier="/us/usc/t99/s2/a/1"><num value="1">(1)</num><content> the structure;</content></paragraph>
</subsection>
<subsection class="indent2 firstIndent-2" identifier="/us/usc/t99/s2/b"><num value="b">(b)</num><heading> Rates</heading><content>
<p class="indent0">A tax determined in accordance with the following table:</p>
<table xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><thead><tr><th>If taxable income is:</th><th>The tax is:</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Not over $36,900</td><td>15% of taxable income.</td></tr></tbody></table>
</content></subsection>
<sourceCredit>(<ref href="/us/pl/112/74/s1">Pub. L. 112–74, § 1</ref>, <date date="2011-12-23">Dec. 23, 2011</date>, <ref href="/us/stat/125/1131">125 Stat. 1131</ref>.)</sourceCredit>
</section>
<section status="repealed" identifier="/us/usc/t99/s3"><num value="3">[§ 3.</num><heading> Repealed. <ref href="/us/pl/99/308/s104/b">Pub. L. 99–308, § 104(b)</ref>, <date date="1986-05-19">May 19, 1986</date>, <ref href="/us/stat/100/459">100 Stat. 459</ref>]</heading><notes type="uscNote">
<note topic="removalDescription"><p>Section related to sample matters.</p></note>
</notes>
</section>
<section identifier="/us/usc/t99/s4 /us/usc/t99/s5"><num value="4, 5">§§ 4, 5.</num><heading> Omitted</heading></section>
<section identifier="/us/usc/t99/s2000e–2"><num value="2000e–2">§ 2000e–2.</num><heading> Unlawful practices</heading><content>
<p class="indent0">It shall be unlawful to quote “<quotedContent><subsection class="indent0"><num value="x">(x)</num><content> a quoted rule</content></subsection></quotedContent>” here.</p>
</content></section>
